<title>GERMANY: German government raises yield on Series 120 Bobls.</title>
<headline>German government raises yield on Series 120 Bobls.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German government has increased the yield on its Series 120 Bundesobligationen bonds, or Bobls, to 4.70 percent from 4.64 percent by lowering the issue price to 101.25 from 101.50, the Bundesbank as issuing agent said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The change took effect at 1100 GMT on Tuesday.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
